    "field": "Climate change impacts on extreme weather",
    "problem": "The impact of rapid seasonal and future warming of the shallow East China Sea on extreme monsoonal rainfall has been unexplored, as global climate models have insufficient resolution to accurately represent the fine-scale sea surface temperatures in such marginal seas.",
    "method": "This study uses a cloud-resolving atmospheric model to simulate a specific torrential rainfall event, altering sea-surface temperature boundary conditions to represent present-day seasonal progression and future warming scenarios derived from global climate models in order to assess their impact on precipitation.",
    "task": "The task is to investigate the impact of seasonal and future warming of the East China Sea on torrential rainfall over western Japan during the Asian summer monsoon, using cloud-resolving atmospheric model simulations.",
