            "relation": "IMPACTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "western Japan",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Here we show through cloud-resolving atmospheric model simulations that observational tendency for torrential rainfall events over western Japan to occur most frequently in July cannot be reproduced without the rapid seasonal warming of ECS.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "extremely heavy rainfall",
            "source_entity_type": "Weather_Event",
            "relation": "IMPACTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Asia",
            "target_entity_type": "Continent",
            "paragraph": "Global climate model projections for the 5th Assessment Reports (AR5) of the Intergovernmental Panel for Climate Change (IPCC) indicate that the global hydrological cycle will intensify in future under the global warming\u00b9, with increasing precipitation over wet climate regions at present, especially in the tropics and summertime subtropical/midlatitude Asia\u00b2, a region of growing economy and population. In these regions summertime precipitation is produced mostly by meso-scale convective systems, which occasionally yield extremely heavy rainfall locally causing serious flooding and/or landslides with casualties.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
