            "target_entity_instance": "Kyushu",
            "target_entity_type": "Country_Subdivision",
            "paragraph": "The moist airflow is most likely to affect the western portion of Kyushu, the westernmost main island of Japan facing ECS.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "torrential rainfall event on July 11-14 2012",
            "source_entity_type": "Weather_Event",
            "relation": "IMPACTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Kyushu",
            "target_entity_type": "Country_Subdivision",
            "paragraph": "An outstanding issue is thus whether the rapid seasonal SST rising in ECS can exert any significant influence on the occurrence of monsoonal heavy rainfall events over Kyushu at present and in future. This issue is addressed through a set of numerical simulations with a cloud-resolving regional atmospheric model\u00b9\u2075, with primary focus on a torrential rainfall event that occurred on the 11th through 14th of July 2012 as a typical test case (see Methods).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "flooding",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Kyushu",
            "target_entity_type": "Country_Subdivision",
            "paragraph": "In that event, a number of weather stations over Kyushu observed rainfall with hourly rate exceeding 25 mm over many hours and 24-hour totals exceeding 100 mm, with records set at eight stations. Consequently, a severe flooding situation caused more than 20 casualties.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
